---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BentoGrid from '../components/BentoGrid.astro';
import BentoCard2Col from '../components/BentoCard2Col.astro';
import BentoCard2Row from '../components/BentoCard2Row.astro';
import HeaderProject from '../components/HeaderProject.astro';

import imgHero from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-hero.png';
import img1 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-comparison.png';
import img2 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-card-holder.png';
import img3 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-checkout.png';
import img4 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-people.png';
import img5 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-cheque-deposit.png';
import img6 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-structure.svg';
import img7 from '../assets/wave-illustrations/spot-sheet.png';
---

<Layout>
	<HeaderProject background="8">
		<Fragment slot="title">Illustrations redesign</Fragment>
		<Fragment slot="body">
			As part of a brand refresh project initiated by the marketing team, I was tasked to rethink our illustration style to make it simpler and more human.
		</Fragment>
		<Fragment slot="media">
			<img src={imgHero.src} alt="Screenshot of the Wave mobile responsive navigation." />
		</Fragment>
	</HeaderProject>

	<BentoGrid dividers>
		<BentoCard2Col>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-3">Project goals</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					In this project our objective was to revamp our illustrations style to reflect our new brand guidelines, reduce cognitive load by moving away from the background blobs used on the old style, and double down on more whimsical elements to convey complex concepts in a simpler way.
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					After landing on a new style that ticked all requirements, with the help of another illustrator, we redesigned all 70 existing illustrations and added 30 more to our library.
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					We also took that opportunity to improve the implementation on code with a new image repository and React component. 
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					All new illustrations on our library follow the four principles listed below.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img1.src} width="90%" alt="A chart of the design system's structure at Wave" />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
	</BentoGrid>
	
	<BentoGrid>
		<BentoCard2Row>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-3">Principles</h2>
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Row>
	</BentoGrid>

	<BentoGrid dividers>
		<BentoCard2Col dividers>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-4">Bring delight</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					Imperfect, looser strokes, and chalk texture humanizes our illustrations as it looks hand-drawn, artisanal.
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					We also changed the style to convey ideas in a more whimsical way, looking to make a, sometimes, abrasive subject more delightful.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img2.src} width="100%" alt="Screenshot of the menu toggle issue on mobile." />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
		<BentoCard2Col >
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-4">Be simple</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					Use less colours and elements. Make the illustration noticeable without taking all the attention from the content they are supporting.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img3.src} width="100%" alt="Screenshot of the old settings placement." />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
	</BentoGrid>

	<BentoGrid dividers>
		<BentoCard2Col dividers>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-4">Represent diversity</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					Our new style is aspirational and diverse. The people that use Wave’s tools should see themselves reflected in the illustrations.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img4.src} width="100%" alt="Screenshot of the menu toggle issue on mobile." />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
		<BentoCard2Col >
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-4">Communicate effectively</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					With the new style, we aim to represent ideas in a fantastical form that enables us to convey complex concepts in a simple way.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img5.src} width="100%" alt="Screenshot of the old settings placement." />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
	</BentoGrid>

	<BentoGrid dividers>
		<BentoCard2Col>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-3">Implementation</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					Before the redesign, all assets were hard-coded on the app. Updating illustrations was a huge endeavour, demanding constant auditing and many developer hours to achieve it.
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					To fix this issue we created a  centralized illustrations repository and a React component to add illustrations on the app. The new structure gives the design systems team flexibility to manage and update illustrations without the support of the product teams.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img6.src} width="90%" alt="A chart of the design system's structure at Wave" />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
	</BentoGrid>

	<BentoGrid dividers>
		<BentoCard2Col>
			<Fragment slot="text">
				<h2 class="text-display-3">Results</h2>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					We did user interviews to measure their perception of the new illustrations. We hada very positive response from our users.
				</p>
				<p class="text-body-default">
					Marketing A/B tested the illustrations on our public site and they achieved 4.6% more signups than a hero variant with a photo.
				</p>
			</Fragment>
			<Fragment slot="media">
				<img src={img7.src} width="100%" alt="A chart of the design system's structure at Wave" />
			</Fragment>
		</BentoCard2Col>
	</BentoGrid>

</Layout>
